    {
      "id": "5znciom",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Keyboard"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Keyboards and mice are the essential primary input and pointing devices used in computing.",
        "Scanners convert physical documents and photographs into digital image formats.",
        "Barcode Readers capture and decode visual barcode patterns into digital alphanumeric data.",
        "OMR, OCR, and MICR are specialized technologies for optical mark, optical character, and magnetic ink recognition."
      ],
      "id": "gub6vt6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tkwvcp2",
      "content": "A keyboard is the most commonly used input device. It is used to type text, numbers, and commands into the computer."
    },
    {
      "id": "1i7gmiy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.1.1 Types of Keys"
    },
    {
      "id": "5e299kp",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Key Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Function</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Alphanumeric Keys</p>",
            "<p>Used for typing letters and numbers.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Function Keys (F1–F12)</p>",
            "<p>Used for special functions depending on the software.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Control Keys</p>",
            "<p>Keys such as Ctrl, Alt, Esc used for command operations.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Navigation Keys</p>",
            "<p>Arrow keys, Home, End used for moving the cursor.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Numeric Keypad</p>",
            "<p>Used for entering numbers quickly.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yho5yf7",
      "content": "Important Exam Points:"
    },
    {
      "id": "fkzf5k6",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Keyboard is the primary input device.",
        "Standard keyboard has around 104 keys.",
        "Function keys are located at the top of the keyboard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "326vdow",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.2 Mouse"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s53i0gp",
      "content": "A mouse is a pointing device used to move the cursor on the computer screen and select objects."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "OMR, OCR, MICR",
      "id": "8ys13e5"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3noi7x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4.2.1 Types of Mouse"
    },
    {
      "id": "n7h6o32",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mechanical Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Uses a rubber ball to detect movement.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Optical Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Uses light sensors to detect movement.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Wireless Mouse</p>",
            "<p>Works without cable using Bluetooth or RF.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4oix3hl",
      "content": "Common Mouse Operations:"
    },
    {
      "id": "midkkuy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Click",
        "Double Click",
        "Right Click",
        "Drag and Drop",
        "Scroll"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g6402u3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.3 Scanner"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l8p91gb",
      "content": "A scanner is an input device used to convert physical documents or images into digital format."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Technology",
        "Full Form",
        "Primary Use Case"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "OMR",
          "Optical Mark Recognition",
          "Evaluating objective exam answer sheets"
        ],
        [
          "OCR",
          "Optical Character Recognition",
          "Digitizing printed books and documents into editable text"
        ],
        [
          "MICR",
          "Magnetic Ink Character Recognition",
          "Processing cheques in banking operations"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "9s3shqu"
    },
    {
      "id": "ybgnxb4",
